\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Scale-free effective regularization strength $r = \beta \,\lVert \nabla _\theta R\rVert _2/\lVert \nabla _\theta \mathrm  {CE}\rVert _2$ at the shared one-epoch CE-only operating point (MNIST/MLP, seed 0). The raw $\beta $ grid is not a shared axis across objectives (SVIB penalizes $\beta \,\mathrm  {KL}^2$, NIB is in nats, DVCCA weights reconstruction too); $r$ is. FGIB-A's row at $a{=}4$ vs $a{=}16$ shows the $a^2/\tau ^2$ coupling explicitly; NIB's $r$ stays below $1.7\times 10^{-3}$ across the grid (its knob does not act).}}{37}{table.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:effective}{{15}{37}{Scale-free effective regularization strength $r = \beta \,\lVert \nabla _\theta R\rVert _2/\lVert \nabla _\theta \mathrm {CE}\rVert _2$ at the shared one-epoch CE-only operating point (MNIST/MLP, seed 0). The raw $\beta $ grid is not a shared axis across objectives (SVIB penalizes $\beta \,\mathrm {KL}^2$, NIB is in nats, DVCCA weights reconstruction too); $r$ is. FGIB-A's row at $a{=}4$ vs $a{=}16$ shows the $a^2/\tau ^2$ coupling explicitly; NIB's $r$ stays below $1.7\times 10^{-3}$ across the grid (its knob does not act)}{table.15}{}}
