\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The stress test on a scale-free axis (MNIST/MLP). Horizontal axis: effective regularization strength $\qopname  \relax o{log}_{10} r$ with $r = \beta \,\lVert \nabla _\theta R\rVert _2/\lVert \nabla _\theta \mathrm  {CE}\rVert _2$ at a shared one-epoch CE-only operating point (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:effective}); vertical axis: the deficit in test accuracy against the deterministic backbone at that $\beta $. NIB's $r$ is below $1.7\times 10^{-3}$ across the grid at this operating point (its knob does not act); SVIB's penalty $\beta \,\operatorname  {KL}^2$ carries different units, so its raw-grid $\beta {=}1$ lands at $r\approx 10^{6.2}$ --- two orders of magnitude beyond any KL-nat objective's grid --- and its collapse there is a scale artifact, not evidence of fragility. Among the KL-nat objectives, VIB, CEB and DVCCA collapse between $r\approx 10^{3.15}$ and $10^{3.23}$, while FGIB-A reaches $r\approx 10^{3.75}$ with zero deficit.}}{38}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:effective}{{2}{38}{The stress test on a scale-free axis (MNIST/MLP). Horizontal axis: effective regularization strength $\log _{10} r$ with $r = \beta \,\lVert \nabla _\theta R\rVert _2/\lVert \nabla _\theta \mathrm {CE}\rVert _2$ at a shared one-epoch CE-only operating point (Table~\ref {tab:effective}); vertical axis: the deficit in test accuracy against the deterministic backbone at that $\beta $. NIB's $r$ is below $1.7\times 10^{-3}$ across the grid at this operating point (its knob does not act); SVIB's penalty $\beta \,\KLd ^2$ carries different units, so its raw-grid $\beta {=}1$ lands at $r\approx 10^{6.2}$ --- two orders of magnitude beyond any KL-nat objective's grid --- and its collapse there is a scale artifact, not evidence of fragility. Among the KL-nat objectives, VIB, CEB and DVCCA collapse between $r\approx 10^{3.15}$ and $10^{3.23}$, while FGIB-A reaches $r\approx 10^{3.75}$ with zero deficit}{figure.2}{}}
