\newlabel{fig:diag}{{3}{40}{Diagnostics on MNIST/MLP. (a) $\log _{10}\kappa (A^{\top }A)$ of the FGIB side head over training, one seed per $\beta $. (b) The trainable-prior variance-race measurement: mean log-variance at the final epoch against $\beta $ for CEB's posterior and prior and VIB's posterior; the dashed line is the initialization $\log \sigma ^2 = 0$}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Long-horizon variance trajectories on MNIST/MLP (400 epochs, early stopping disabled, one seed, full validation set per epoch). CEB's posterior and prior log-variances drift down together --- the trainable-prior race in its measured direction; DCEB's prior log-variance drifts \emph  {up} at $\beta {=}1$ --- the corrected sign of Corollary\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {cor:family} --- while its $\beta {=}10$ collapse occurs with the variance near initialization; VIB's posterior holds at the initialization --- the fixed prior restores the variance, so no race exists (Remark\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {rem:vib-prior}); FGIB's posterior is the flat zero line --- the fixed point of Result\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {res:varfreeze}, held exactly for the whole run.}}{40}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:longtrain}{{4}{40}{Long-horizon variance trajectories on MNIST/MLP (400 epochs, early stopping disabled, one seed, full validation set per epoch). CEB's posterior and prior log-variances drift down together --- the trainable-prior race in its measured direction; DCEB's prior log-variance drifts \emph {up} at $\beta {=}1$ --- the corrected sign of Corollary~\ref {cor:family} --- while its $\beta {=}10$ collapse occurs with the variance near initialization; VIB's posterior holds at the initialization --- the fixed prior restores the variance, so no race exists (Remark~\ref {rem:vib-prior}); FGIB's posterior is the flat zero line --- the fixed point of Result~\ref {res:varfreeze}, held exactly for the whole run}{figure.4}{}}
